#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092040 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "57034318-5a6e-53f6-a8d3-ae8c61692947" :question/math-academy-id "e-641" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/0bb9e5e7315d4bcd5fc21700fdd2597f6d9b585a109145de53c6f94e9530eabf.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi$ (shown in blue in the picture above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now use the half-angle formula $1-\\cos\\theta =2\\sin^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$ to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={-4\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092070 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "8b8e3c66-fc60-57ac-baf7-0661e213d01e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7400" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/e5647c0f19727d1e626e637464cc57444e0bc0f2f8e99a4afd15d3c3631dc3f0.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the arc length of the polar curve $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi,$ shown in blue in the diagram above." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} =-7\\cos(7\\theta)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}+(-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+49{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+1+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "974ca213-2172-5e9c-8725-e36303616bb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384873} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea815d7-5176-5026-9d14-50609b292b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+6{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384874} {:answer/id #uuid "6e533383-5c44-55d5-bbe5-0ca489de7f0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )-6{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384875} {:answer/id #uuid "91cefaee-7f3d-5552-9d31-85ee9e1b2e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )-{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384876} {:answer/id #uuid "90f9b78e-20e1-5156-b4ec-5e79a23a7a1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974ca213-2172-5e9c-8725-e36303616bb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384873} :answer-field/id #uuid "46de6714-54ea-554b-9b0d-7ced1a3e4f2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc7335a9-16fc-51fb-856d-48780c80c78e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103832" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))^{2}+(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )+36{sin}^{2}⁡(6\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d7f5e70-2f71-54cd-9319-8c3a6c54a7b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384880} {:answer/id #uuid "eea7efe9-c899-52a9-b469-e59474f9b0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384881} {:answer/id #uuid "bd8ed757-247d-5d0a-ac56-25fb9552df02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384882} {:answer/id #uuid "781ee685-3944-5237-b948-c18d06a01f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384883} {:answer/id #uuid "4d751d74-87d1-5ad2-9e5c-7dc9050e2a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d7f5e70-2f71-54cd-9319-8c3a6c54a7b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384880} :answer-field/id #uuid "c028f2ad-eb7b-557c-85a0-12b80ab13ee1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ed037d3-a424-5f4d-8851-f39873da08ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-103834" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/1bd01b4fe70a497cc66811a2d5b070908221b9932655ee396d9a8039471702c2.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cd58626-f106-57af-9e9b-6b7850a52c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384887} {:answer/id #uuid "77067f41-cff1-55a6-ac42-d1cde970f3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384888} {:answer/id #uuid "5b6d4286-d426-5db8-b46d-04d6318f2ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384889} {:answer/id #uuid "a7367d03-86ba-5bc7-bf5a-2cc55ad56c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384890} {:answer/id #uuid "1730c364-d722-5384-bbf4-eee62d4725a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1730c364-d722-5384-bbf4-eee62d4725a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384891} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab7be4b7-a6bd-5f58-b416-5153b8789e82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c659d13d-a024-51d5-b83b-b004bef94416" :question/math-academy-id "q-15136" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(1+{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2{e}^{\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9841d5a0-2d6c-5f87-a27a-f94eefabc095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 4θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089539} {:answer/id #uuid "29dd10e3-97bd-56a6-b470-31427419f7fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{4θ^{2} + 2θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089540} {:answer/id #uuid "33a3e6d0-52bd-58d1-a159-6de1f2c26ef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{θ^{2} + θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089541} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbdd8df-eace-5463-a068-bbed35d03037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 2θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089542} {:answer/id #uuid "64f79122-83f5-593c-b841-41de68986368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 2θ + 2}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fbdd8df-eace-5463-a068-bbed35d03037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 2θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089542} :answer-field/id #uuid "0639070a-f499-59b7-b57a-59e78c70795f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd646452-89ff-5f38-8817-208b877e41c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-15144" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/4b03822d65ec9f5bea3a1e47d25e4831470754fa09cef510e7c452cc292e9e40.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\theta {e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\theta {e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={e}^{\\theta }+\\theta {e}^{\\theta }=(1+\\theta ){e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\theta {e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{((1+\\theta ){e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}{e}^{2\\theta }+(1+2\\theta +{\\theta }^{2}){e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1){e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\theta }\\sqrt{2{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4db64b8-39e3-5c3b-bc74-edf065084c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{-\\pi /4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354601} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf02204-23e8-5e54-a4dd-0835514589fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354602} {:answer/id #uuid "f2cc63ef-146d-5d35-9c03-aa861095956e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354603} {:answer/id #uuid "7de1217e-7df7-5c94-8bd2-95e6bd28e197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{\\pi /4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354604} {:answer/id #uuid "64de7071-e0e2-52b9-a70e-48a7c56e596b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2cc63ef-146d-5d35-9c03-aa861095956e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354603} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b447a4-4384-55a0-831a-bdb7fbf86d1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eeba4fa8-124a-54c9-ba6c-4f189488c740" :question/math-academy-id "q-20070" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/fa1c1c3ae2769f45854de4f0b00fc394fccb40b40704cfd09e6eb11eee3c07af.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=3{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{e}^{2\\theta }+9{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{18{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38e024c3-2f36-51b4-9808-c9b74ce7d6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\pi/8}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384894} {:answer/id #uuid "1de9c005-5309-53f4-8684-874cd3ffc09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\pi/8}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38e024c3-2f36-51b4-9808-c9b74ce7d6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{\\pi/8}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384894} :answer-field/id #uuid "e562ab53-baf2-5d81-ac32-7a5ffe8bfac7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd251789-4dc6-5eb3-a93a-44a9735de025" :question/math-academy-id "q-347926" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/2da83e2ec620d3920c4378a77785a9ef2802dd1d06badcf4852be2263f68264e.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=6{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{8}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=6\\sqrt{2}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=6{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=6{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{{(6{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(6{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{36{e}^{2\\theta }+36{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{72{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /8} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /8}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /8}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9813fe1-459a-5e43-be3b-d8816ecf0ba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\ln(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384898} {:answer/id #uuid "a89feb5d-3bfe-547c-ab24-a7ffc179252c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9813fe1-459a-5e43-be3b-d8816ecf0ba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\ln(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384898} :answer-field/id #uuid "2af181e2-36db-5731-ae7a-c207a459de58" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "607472b8-7420-5238-a280-73715b78e8a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-353605" :question/problem "Find the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r={3}^{\\theta /4}$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 4.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}$\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡3+16}$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={3}^{\\theta /4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={3}^{\\theta /4}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{{({3}^{\\theta /4})}^{2}+{({3}^{\\theta /4}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{{3}^{\\theta /2}+{3}^{\\theta /2}\\cdot \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{(1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}){3}^{\\theta /2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{3}^{\\theta /4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {3}^{\\theta /4}\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot ({3}^{1}-{3}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡3}{16}}\\cdot \\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡3+16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93df36f3-915e-5cde-8a42-7c7104d64333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/3}\\sqrt{\\cos^{2} (2θ) - 4\\sin^{2} (2θ)}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090726} {:answer/id #uuid "1e29cc71-a41f-5216-8d01-962a8be26486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/3}\\sqrt{\\cos^{2} (2θ) + 4\\sin^{2} (2θ)}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090727} {:answer/id #uuid "2287eb2f-2880-563e-9be6-7fd84bcc3b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/3}\\sqrt{\\cos^{2} (2θ) + \\sin^{2} (2θ)}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090728} {:answer/id #uuid "60bbc524-aa19-5147-af9f-40164bbb7f09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/3}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2} (2θ) + 2\\cos^{2} (2θ)}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090729} {:answer/id #uuid "690839b5-2223-5245-a4b7-981d0e86fa0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/3}\\sqrt{\\sin^{2} (2θ) + 4\\cos^{2} (2θ)}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e29cc71-a41f-5216-8d01-962a8be26486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∫_{0}^{π/3}\\sqrt{\\cos^{2} (2θ) + 4\\sin^{2} (2θ)}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090727} :answer-field/id #uuid "d01b766a-0765-5803-8f6d-997684170fa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1df0a62-d91d-5d2f-932b-891ad126ab27" :question/math-academy-id "q-51198" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af5078a4-a99b-5126-bc81-39bc1715b7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384902} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b4ea04-76a3-51fe-86c7-3f2053f855a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384903} {:answer/id #uuid "05ec77a2-d017-55b6-b85d-3f8a362803c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{e}^{\\pi /6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384904} {:answer/id #uuid "0d151997-d40b-5d02-865e-a135456459e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384905} {:answer/id #uuid "706b5e30-545c-5187-8dd2-f5d9a963fd30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5({e}^{\\pi /6}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af5078a4-a99b-5126-bc81-39bc1715b7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384902} :answer-field/id #uuid "671656e0-65f6-5d5d-b743-d7612dbb15be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c78602b-4403-575e-8166-123d9c1454a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-51201" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/8076c5991e4c66bb505fa1800ce3d78fab0fc115560ef59efb72e6776976c977.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=5{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=5{e}^{\\theta },$ wehave\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(5{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(5{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{25{e}^{2\\theta }+25{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\sqrt{50{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /6}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6064233-ed38-5ef3-8349-1dd3a03c75b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091680} {:answer/id #uuid "db306417-a82a-5664-b0d9-2362a93d761e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091681} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1e274f-8eb5-5481-b78c-b5fbba99795e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091682} {:answer/id #uuid "6c96387a-f2f3-5c59-a3a3-92a83acc5088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091683} {:answer/id #uuid "74a7db6a-2d70-5ff8-b64d-297fa28f56d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db306417-a82a-5664-b0d9-2362a93d761e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091681} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1c56fba-9bc3-51b4-a438-d20c93c6b9e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfaa6223-b113-5398-adeb-e8d8b6d36965" :question/math-academy-id "q-9532" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077889/assets/085be1e624ae99afee256d2a9591f17d2f33f688364b6e59fdcd7c415206bda7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta {|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
